# Col Fenwick - farmer of Harrowfield (Act 1 village).
# First talk: descriptive INTRO (start); completing it sets TSC_MetCol
# and later visits enter at hub. Flesh out the hub freely.
# Compile with:  scripts\Compile-Dialogue.ps1

dialogue TSC_Dialogue_Col

# Night visits: asleep node preempts everything (entries in order).
entry asleep if sleeping()

entry hub if flag(TSC_MetCol)

== start ==
The man by the small cottage is doing nothing at all, and doing it with great skill: arms crossed, back to the wall, watching the road. He nods when you're close enough, unhurried, as if he had seen you coming since yesterday.

"Col Fenwick. The small plot's ours, mine and Bryn's." He considers, and evidently decides you've earned one more sentence. "You walk like the pass. Rough country makes that walk."

* "It does. Well met, Col." -> hub
    do flag(TSC_MetCol)
* "You watch that road like you're expecting something." -> hub
    do flag(TSC_MetCol)
* "Just passing." -> end

== hub ==
Col nods at you, unhurried.

"Roads bring all sorts lately. Hope you're one of the better sorts."

* "What do you know about a nearby sanguophage crypt?" -> crypt
    if flag(TSC_RitesDone)
* "I found an old journal in the caves under the well. Unsigned. Does it mean anything to you?" -> journal
    if flag(TSC_WeatheredJournalRead)
* "I'm looking for work." -> ridge_offer_survivor
    if quest_succeeded(TSC_Side_Raiders) and not quest_active(TSC_Side_RidgeLight) and not quest_succeeded(TSC_Side_RidgeLight)
* "I'm looking for work." -> ridge_offer_band
    if not quest_succeeded(TSC_Side_Raiders) and not quest_active(TSC_Side_RidgeLight) and not quest_succeeded(TSC_Side_RidgeLight)
* "The ridge light still burns, Col." -> ridge_progress
    if quest_active(TSC_Side_RidgeLight)
* "Just passing through." -> end

== asleep ==
Col sleeps facing the door. Of course he does. His breathing doesn't change as you approach, but you'd bet a day's rations he knows exactly where you're standing.

* [Shake them awake.] -> woken
    do wake()
* [Leave them to their rest.] -> end

== woken ==
Col's eyes are open before your hand leaves his shoulder. His grip finds something under the bedroll that isn't a blanket, then relaxes.

"...Courier." He settles back. "Don't do that to a man who's stood watches. Morning will do."

* "Sorry. Go back to sleep." -> end
* "Morning, then." -> end

== crypt ==
Col is quiet for a moment longer than the question needs. When he answers, it's flat and final.

"No. I watch the road, not the hills." A beat. "And I'd keep it that way, if I were you."

* "Noted, Col." -> hub

== journal ==
Col's jaw tightens.

"Caves under the well," he repeats, flat. "I stand watch on this village and I did not know the ground under it was hollow."

"A journal is paper. Paper doesn't worry me. Take it to the elder; old things are his."

* "I understand." -> hub

== ridge_offer_survivor ==
Col considers you for a while, then makes a decision you can watch happen.

"Three nights now, there's been a light on the ridge." He nods at the hills without looking at them. "You broke the raider band in the pass; I heard. But somebody walked away from that, and whoever it is has found friends, and now they sit up there. Counting our chimneys."

* "I'll go put the light out." -> hub
    do give_quest(TSC_Side_RidgeLight); affinity(+5)
* "Maybe it's shepherds." -> hub

== ridge_offer_band ==
Col considers you for a while, then makes a decision you can watch happen.

"Three nights now, there's been a light on the ridge." He nods at the hills without looking at them. "The crownless bandits work the pass roads. A light that comes back three nights running isn't a campfire, it's a *post*. And a post above a village is a measuring stick."

* "I'll go put the light out." -> hub
    do give_quest(TSC_Side_RidgeLight); affinity(+5)
* "Maybe it's shepherds." -> hub

== ridge_progress ==
"Aye." Col doesn't need it explained. "Burned again last night, two fingers left of the notch rock. They're patient." A beat. "Be less patient than them."

* "Working on it." -> hub
